// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// i18n.js — lightweight localization layer for the State Combat Analytics
// clone. No React/build-step here (see app.js's header comment), so this is
// a small hand-rolled equivalent of i18next rather than the library itself:
// same shape (namespaced dotted keys, per-locale dictionaries, a fallback
// chain, a single t() lookup function used everywhere instead of scattering
// per-component language checks) adapted to this app's plain
// innerHTML-template rendering style.
//
// SOURCE OF TRUTH: the logged-in member's `preferredLanguage` field (see
// data.js SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES / DEFAULT_LANGUAGE_CODE) — the exact same
// profile value Create Account, My Account, and Admin's member editor all
// read and write. This file does not introduce a second language value.
//
// HOW RE-RENDERING WORKS: this app has no virtual DOM — every page is a
// fresh `innerHTML = \`...${t("some.key")}...\`` template string evaluated
// at render time (see router() in app.js). So changing the active locale
// needs no reactive plumbing: t() just reads currentLocale() fresh on every
// call, and calling renderShell()+router() again (already the standard
// pattern used everywhere else in this codebase after a state change, e.g.
// the Admin "Save" handler) re-evaluates every template with the new
// language. setLocale() below does exactly that.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Only user-facing INTERFACE text belongs in here — never Gamer Names,
// Gamer IDs, Alliance Tags, other user-entered text, or game-specific
// values like T10 / FC5 / T12 (those are data, not UI copy, and stay as
// typed everywhere in every language, per the localization spec).
